464: ## IE.6. Scalar-order independence and exact local values
465: 
466: The selected-cusp fan in this argument is the initial
467: vertical-edge fan or its literal reflected fan under
468: \((Z,V)\mapsto(Z^{-1},P^aV)\). In either marking the
469: physical delta circle has the already specified
470: \((-1,+1)\) fixed-curve model, and the selected-unit
471: transport in IE.2 closes that same fan. The admitted
472: source/cap sectors are \((a,b)=(1,2)\), \(m=4p\),
473: and \((a,b)=(2,1)\), \(m=4p-1\), with \(p\ge1\),
474: their actual \(n=\pm1\) norm markings, and the
475: retained integral \(d\delta\) twist. No comparison
476: with a further flopped fan is used here.
477: 
478: Over \(U\) the ordinary suspension, with
479: no linearization zero, is an actual family
480: over the product of a source annulus and
481: a small scalar annulus:
482: \[
483:                    B_\lambda=2(-1)^{b+1}\lambda q_*U_a^b.
484: \]
485: There is no finite cap in this local
486: family, so every integer scalar winding
487: is a closed local loop. Its source-base
488: boundary family extends over the source
489: disc, with the actual periods and Cartier
490: frames. Choose IE.1's transport on this
491: entire product.
492: 
493: A pair of pants mapping into this
494: product realizes the based-loop identity
495: \[
496:  (\epsilon\text{ turn},N\text{ scalar turns})
497:    =(\epsilon\text{ turn},0)+(0,N\text{ scalar turns}).    \tag{IE.14}
498: \]
499: Pull back the actual local family and
500: quotient its free physical circle.
501: This is a seven-dimensional bordism
502: of the mapping-torus pieces. Glue the
503: source-base boundary collars by the
504: full-product transport. The fixed-source
505: scalar-loop boundary is exactly the
506: reference piece of IE.1 and cancels.
507: Thus the closed relative collision
508: boundaries \(Q_{\rm rel}(N)\) and
509: \(Q_{\rm rel}(0)\) are bordant with
510: their actual Euler line. Their
511: characteristic difference is independent
512: of \(N\). This is a literal parameter
513: product and collar construction; no
514: division of a covered sphere class occurs.
515: 
516: For any admitted cap, its exterior
517: source/root/line family extends over
518: the source disc. IE.2 cancels it with
519: the constant exterior. Hence this
520: same local relative boundary represents
521: the fixed-scalar source loop for that
522: completed family. It suffices to use
523: the two fully executed orders \(N=8\)
524: for \((a,b)=(1,2)\), and \(N=6\) for
525: \((a,b)=(2,1)\):
526: \[
527:  \begin{array}{c|rrr}
528:  (a,b,N)&\text{interior/H}&N\text{ E doubles}&\text{total}\\ \hline
529:  (1,2,8)&2&-2&0\\
530:  (2,1,6)&5&-6&-1 .
531:  \end{array}                                           \tag{IE.15}
532: \]
533: Independent executions at \(N=4,12\)
534: in the first case and \(N=3,9\) in
535: the second give the same relative
536: sums. They check the arithmetic;
537: the independence proof is (IE.14).
538: 
539: By (IE.13), the fixed-scalar marked infinity
540: Jin differences are respectively \(0\) and \(+1\).
541: Apply P3F.22's proved Jin-to-\(\Theta_7\) transfer
542: to the two actual completed boundary mapping
543: tori: on each, IE.2 has made the specified conifold
544: replacement, transported the same positive meridian,
545: and retained the actual Euler line of its free circle
546: bundle. To select their actual return maps, prescribe
547: the product connection on the common selected tube
548: in IE.2's closed Cox product, extend it to a connection
549: on the actual parameter family, and average over
550: the physical delta circle. The prescribed product
551: connection remains unchanged under that averaging.
552: After the conifold replacement its return is a
553: diffeomorphism \(f\) of \(Y=S^2\times S^3\), equal
554: to the identity on the prescribed tube. The actual
555: Euler line extends around the family, so \(f\)
556: preserves its primitive class \(x\in H^2(Y;\mathbb Z)\).
557: The return preserves orientation; the perfect
558: pairing \(H^2\otimes H^3\to H^5\) then shows that
559: it preserves \(H^3\) as well. Thus \(f\in I(Y)\).
560: 
561: On the complement of that tube, P3F.22's Hopf lift
562: is literally the physical return lift supplied by
563: this delta-equivariant connection and its preserved
564: Euler line. On the tube it is the same identity
565: extension in the proved conifold/Hopf collar
566: construction. Consequently its \(\lambda(f)\) is
567: the actual clutched sphere of this parameter return.
568: This identifies the return map and its lift before
569: using the characteristic polynomial. Their
570: characteristic integers are
571: \(\int(4x^3-p_1x)/24\) in the Jin convention.
572: The transfer sends their difference to that integer
573: modulo 28. The pair-of-pants map (IE.14) identifies
574: the difference of these actual returns with the
575: fixed-scalar positive epsilon source loop. Thus
576: its oriented sphere class is \(0\) for \((a,b)=(1,2)\)
577: and \(1\) for \((a,b)=(2,1)\), in each of the two
578: specified vertical-edge fan markings. This conclusion
579: does not assign either source-zero fan return.
580: 
